The tile typeface bundled at src/assets/atkinson-next-500.woff2 is a subset of

    Atkinson Hyperlegible Next
    Copyright Braille Institute of America, Inc.

licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, the full text of which is
available at https://openfontlicense.org and alongside the font at
https://www.brailleinstitute.org/freefont.

It is drawn to make characters hard to confuse with one another — a serifed I, a
foot on the 1, a mark through the 0 — which is why this app uses it: those are
exactly the characters a camera cannot otherwise separate from a fragment of a
tile's printed border.

Weight 500 rather than 700, and that is measured rather than taste. At the size
the recogniser sees, 700 closes the counters — the hole in an A comes out eight
pixels across, in an 8 sixteen — and those holes are what separate H from N and
O from D. 500 keeps nearly all of the light weight's counter area with enough
stroke to survive the downsampling.

The font is subset to the 39 characters this app prints on its tile sheet and is
distributed under the terms of that licence, separately from the MIT licence
covering the rest of frosmo (see LICENSE).
